{"id": "EUVD-2026-103932", "enisaUuid": "c1692515-f640-378d-807a-bead996620a8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: ad4030: fix invalid oversampling_ratio validation\n\nIn ad4030_set_avg_frame_len(), the logarithm is calculated before input\nvalidation. Passing zero or negative values leads to an undefined result\nfrom ilog2().\n\nValidate that the input is strictly positive prior to computing its\nlogarithm.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b0cc4e32599f59c994a60743f53fc72cb2979f4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ca6dcbaa68c5e6dc4df171a32c5822e1a4c66c1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d615210564205993e8f0e7ccb57cc2e66b7d5706"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m2wg-6jmr-mfrp", "CVE-2026-98678"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "221fdce0-5631-3be9-a487-e668637bacfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "949abd1ca5a4342d9fb8c774035222e65dd1cfe4 <d615210564205993e8f0e7ccb57cc2e66b7d5706"}, {"id": "6038b1a5-0521-3e0f-833c-97914f03e3b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "949abd1ca5a4342d9fb8c774035222e65dd1cfe4 <6b0cc4e32599f59c994a60743f53fc72cb2979f4"}, {"id": "89628448-d28d-32bd-9d04-f38c7d208973", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "96a3f026-423b-34e5-a06a-14728ee6ee6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b312732c-2138-3187-9bed-ad7a2499ca02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c7224223-29af-30da-8c6d-98a9da30e186", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "949abd1ca5a4342d9fb8c774035222e65dd1cfe4 <6ca6dcbaa68c5e6dc4df171a32c5822e1a4c66c1"}, {"id": "f18be278-098e-3582-a